I lot of times it's necessary to do n11s or whatever to search a spot
for awhile or to waste time (i.e. if you're doing a sacfest and you're
waiting for monsters).  However, oftentimes you're interrupted in the
middle of this, especially if it's a long interval.  What the game
should do is, if you're interrupted in the middle of resting/searching
by a monster appearing or a negative going away (hallucination,
blindness, whatever), then the game should print out how many turns
elapsed out of the total you wanted to rest for.

This way you won't have to carefully keep track of the turn numbers if
you're trying to wait a specific amount of time but keep getting
interrupted.  I don't think this should be that hard to implement.

